WEBVTT

01:54.864 --> 01:56.032
Oh, God.

01:56.116 --> 01:57.408
Look.

01:57.492 --> 01:58.368
- That's her, isn't it?
- Right?

01:58.451 --> 01:59.619
See? What'd I tell you? It's her.

02:00.620 --> 02:02.122
- That druggie girl, Cha Soo-jung.
- Like, what's her deal?

02:02.205 --> 02:03.706
Well, shit.

02:03.790 --> 02:05.333
- Why are we meeting here, of all places?
- Fishnet tights? Is she for real?

02:05.416 --> 02:06.334
Isn't she embarrassed?

02:08.378 --> 02:09.420
Who's that dude?

02:09.504 --> 02:10.505
Burger alright?

02:10.588 --> 02:11.464
Is that her sugar daddy?

02:11.548 --> 02:12.507
- Why'd she get kicked out, again? Weed?
- This is my first meal of

02:12.590 --> 02:14.634
- the day, you little brat.
- I heard "meth."

02:14.717 --> 02:16.803
- Shit, you bitches I can hear you.
- Oh, no.

02:16.886 --> 02:18.096
Kid, you've gotta calm down.

02:18.179 --> 02:19.180
- Hey!
- Let's go.

02:19.264 --> 02:20.056
Hey, come on. Fuck her.

02:20.140 --> 02:21.015
- What a freak.
- Nah, it's fine.

02:21.099 --> 02:21.975
- Crazy bitch.
- No, no don't go!

02:22.058 --> 02:23.143
You girls can keep eating.

02:23.226 --> 02:24.644
- No, come back!
- Fucking bitch.

02:24.727 --> 02:26.104
- Listen here, Detective.
- What a loser.

02:27.188 --> 02:28.815
Well I looked out for
her during our juvie days

02:28.898 --> 02:29.941
And all

02:30.024 --> 02:30.942
But not anymore

02:31.609 --> 02:32.944
That's all in the past

02:33.027 --> 02:34.904
What the fuck do i have
to do with that bitch?

02:35.697 --> 02:39.242
I don't give a flying bitch shit
about Mr. Lee, but you're so damn fucking

02:39.325 --> 02:40.618
- Annoying.
- Hey!

02:40.702 --> 02:41.578
Keep it together, alright?

02:47.584 --> 02:48.501
Damn.

02:54.174 --> 02:55.049
Soo-jung.

02:55.133 --> 02:57.093
You think I called 'cause I
love hanging out with you?

02:57.177 --> 02:58.052
Huh?

02:58.136 --> 02:59.929
You… told me that you got a call from
that bitch seeing if you'd work for Mr.

03:00.013 --> 03:01.890
Lee right.

03:04.058 --> 03:05.268
I'd never have you do anything dangerous.

03:05.852 --> 03:07.228
Just do the job interview,

03:07.312 --> 03:08.229
Okay?

03:09.147 --> 03:09.981
Use this to call me.

03:13.902 --> 03:15.111
I promise this'll be the last time, okay?

03:18.406 --> 03:19.949
Do you feel a little bad right now?

03:20.867 --> 03:21.784
Well, I-

03:22.410 --> 03:23.411
Jeez, you're such a little brat.

03:23.995 --> 03:25.121
You do have a conscience.

03:26.539 --> 03:28.791
They'll take me to the
terminal from Yongsan Station.

03:29.584 --> 03:30.585
Why are they making you go to the
station if they're taking you to the

03:30.668 --> 03:32.503
terminal? Why not go straight there?

03:32.587 --> 03:34.214
You can go, if you're so curious.

03:34.297 --> 03:35.215
I would if I could.

03:35.298 --> 03:36.216
How long will it take?

03:36.758 --> 03:38.009
They said two hours at the most.

03:40.094 --> 03:41.221
Two hours…

03:41.304 --> 03:42.555
Okay.

03:42.639 --> 03:43.806
Let's meet at nine in the Yongsan lobby.

03:43.890 --> 03:45.225
Alright?

03:45.308 --> 03:46.476
You know what?

03:46.559 --> 03:48.519
I know everybody else
thinks I'm a crazy bitch…

03:49.979 --> 03:52.106
I hope you never call
me that, though, okay?

03:54.025 --> 03:54.943
Crazy bitch.

03:56.277 --> 03:58.446
I wanna have a nice
life, like anyone else.

03:58.529 --> 03:59.447
Why do you do drugs, then?

04:00.823 --> 04:02.200
Because the world is shit.

04:02.283 --> 04:04.494
- And it's perfect for everyone but you?
- No one but me does drugs?

04:05.703 --> 04:07.205
Mature behavior, smartass

04:07.288 --> 04:08.915
Hey, sit down. Hey!

04:10.583 --> 04:11.417
You want a burger?

04:12.418 --> 04:13.670
Now you think to ask me that?

04:15.213 --> 04:16.130
Don't leave now.

04:16.881 --> 04:17.799
Mm-hmm.

04:24.097 --> 04:27.225
Lee Hak-seung, chairman of Ewoo Shipping,
died of cardiac arrest yesterday morning.

04:27.308 --> 04:29.060
Even on the second day of his funeral,

04:29.143 --> 04:30.645
Political, economic, and cultural
figures continued to come pay their

04:30.728 --> 04:32.563
respects.

04:32.647 --> 04:35.066
After founding Ewoo
Shipping, Lee was at the forefront

04:35.149 --> 04:37.777
Of Korea's economic
growth in the eighties.

04:37.860 --> 04:39.487
He went on to lead various
national projects in the nineties.

04:39.570 --> 04:40.989
- Well, shit.
- Jesus is coming!

04:41.072 --> 04:42.532
He was regarded as one of the
most influential businessmen

04:42.615 --> 04:44.200
- For God so loved the world,
- in Korea.

04:44.284 --> 04:45.285
He gave His only Son…

04:45.368 --> 04:46.244
- However, after his death,
- And who shall…

04:46.327 --> 04:47.245
believe in him…

04:47.328 --> 04:49.580
His primary care provider made a
public statement that Lee hadn't shown

04:49.664 --> 04:51.749
Signs of health problems before his death.

04:51.833 --> 04:54.460
Consequently, people are
questioning the cause of his death.

04:55.253 --> 04:56.879
In response to these reactions,

04:56.963 --> 04:58.506
Ewoo Shipping has condemned

04:58.589 --> 05:00.049
Such baseless rumors.

05:00.925 --> 05:01.843
However, online…

05:30.830 --> 05:31.748
Soo-jung.

05:32.582 --> 05:33.750
Soo-jung!

05:34.375 --> 05:35.376
Hey!

05:35.460 --> 05:37.253
Soo-jung! L'il brat!

05:37.337 --> 05:38.254
Hey!

05:38.338 --> 05:39.464
Open your eyes!

05:39.547 --> 05:40.465
Soo-jung!

05:42.592 --> 05:43.634
Hey!

05:43.718 --> 05:44.635
Come on.

05:51.768 --> 05:53.019
Increase IV dosage.

05:53.102 --> 05:54.437
Keep checking her vitals.

05:54.520 --> 05:55.813
Yes, ma'am. Raising it to a third.

05:57.982 --> 05:58.900
You're her guardian?

06:00.026 --> 06:01.069
No, I'm police.

06:01.152 --> 06:02.487
I meant, is she your kid?

06:04.655 --> 06:06.699
If you're police,
please bring her guardian.

06:07.367 --> 06:08.284
She's critical right now.

06:09.911 --> 06:10.870
Get me Ativan.

06:10.953 --> 06:11.871
Here.

06:21.964 --> 06:22.799
You little brat.

06:33.184 --> 06:34.102
Huh?

06:36.771 --> 06:37.688
Shit.

06:49.200 --> 06:50.118
Eight?

06:50.785 --> 06:51.702
Eight?

06:53.913 --> 06:54.872
Cardiac arrest!

06:54.956 --> 06:56.040
She's in cardiac arrest!

06:56.749 --> 06:58.000
- Hey, Soo-jung!
- Activate Code Blue

06:58.084 --> 06:58.918
And prepare for CPR.

07:00.878 --> 07:02.004
- Please leave.
- Oh…

07:02.088 --> 07:02.839
Yeah.

07:02.922 --> 07:04.173
One, Two,

07:04.257 --> 07:04.966
Three,

07:05.049 --> 07:05.716
Four,

07:05.800 --> 07:06.717
Five,

07:06.801 --> 07:07.427
- Get me epinephrine.
- Six,

07:07.510 --> 07:07.969
Seven,

07:08.052 --> 07:08.469
Yes, Doctor.

07:08.553 --> 07:09.053
Eight,

07:09.137 --> 07:09.720
Nine,

07:09.804 --> 07:10.388
Ten…

07:24.026 --> 07:26.070
Let's hear your
pathetic excuse of a report.

07:27.196 --> 07:28.156
- Sir.
- You're a team leader.

07:28.239 --> 07:30.032
People say you're
getting cloudy, from being in

07:30.116 --> 07:30.950
Narcotics too long.

07:31.701 --> 07:32.785
"Make a new team," they'd say.

07:32.869 --> 07:34.412
I defended you, and look at me now.

07:34.495 --> 07:35.413
I'm a fool.

07:36.080 --> 07:38.082
Do you know what Mr. Lee
looks like? His name or age?

07:38.166 --> 07:39.542
He might not even be a "mister."

07:40.418 --> 07:42.295
For two years you bust your
ass, with nothing to show.

07:43.212 --> 07:44.213
And now there's this?

07:44.297 --> 07:45.840
You used a minor, and got her murdered.

07:47.425 --> 07:48.342
Look…

07:48.426 --> 07:49.594
Soo-jung…

07:49.677 --> 07:50.595
Was like a niece to me.

07:50.678 --> 07:51.721
I don't care

07:51.804 --> 07:54.265
That you two cared about each
other or any sentimental crap.

07:54.974 --> 07:56.100
Whatever.

07:56.184 --> 07:57.143
You're outta your mind, Jo.

07:57.226 --> 07:58.728
I'll have Team Two take the
case. You're out as of today.

07:58.811 --> 08:00.980
- Sir, I'm going to catch Mr. Lee.
- You've lost it, you crazy bastard!

08:01.063 --> 08:03.232
Maybe, but please just
keep me on this case.

08:05.276 --> 08:07.528
Killing Soo-jung was that
bastard's warning message for me.

08:08.571 --> 08:09.780
"I murdered your puppet."

08:11.449 --> 08:12.617
"You better stay away, you asshole."

08:13.993 --> 08:15.036
I have to be the one to get him.

08:17.747 --> 08:19.040
Mmm. Sir, I will…

08:20.374 --> 08:21.292
Get Mr. Lee.

09:22.103 --> 09:23.312
Ma'am!

09:23.396 --> 09:24.313
Excuse me!

09:34.991 --> 09:35.950
What floor is narcotics?

09:40.371 --> 09:41.289
Oh Yeon-ok.

09:45.167 --> 09:47.044
You waltzed in here on your own?

09:49.088 --> 09:50.673
I'm flattered you know who I am, but

09:50.756 --> 09:51.799
Where are your manners?

09:53.259 --> 09:54.552
You know me?

09:54.635 --> 09:56.304
Yeon-ok Paint's Chairwoman Oh.

09:56.387 --> 09:58.014
You're Mr. Lee's power broker…

09:58.097 --> 09:59.015
That right?

10:00.391 --> 10:02.768
You look like a thug,
yet you did your homework.

10:05.771 --> 10:06.856
So you want Mr. Lee?

10:08.608 --> 10:09.817
Get him!

10:09.900 --> 10:10.818
I'll help you capture him.

10:12.111 --> 10:13.070
In return,

10:13.154 --> 10:14.280
Let me hide out here.

10:16.574 --> 10:18.451
Mr. Lee wanted me to
die today, and I didn't.

10:19.243 --> 10:20.578
He will look for me,

10:20.661 --> 10:22.163
If he finds out I survived.

10:28.961 --> 10:30.755
- Front door…
- Mmhmm.

10:40.681 --> 10:41.599
Oh.

10:48.147 --> 10:49.023
So…

10:49.106 --> 10:51.400
He built a factory in a
place like this. Interesting.

10:51.942 --> 10:52.860
The list of casualties.

10:53.486 --> 10:55.488
No wonder we could
never quite track it down.

10:57.948 --> 10:58.991
Just look at these fatalities.

10:59.992 --> 11:00.910
They're all here.

11:01.577 --> 11:03.621
This was supposed to be a board meeting?

11:05.039 --> 11:06.374
They're all dead now, huh?

11:06.457 --> 11:09.710
"Explosive was an ammonium nitrate
bomb with an electronic detonating

11:09.794 --> 11:10.961
- Device, uh…"
- The bomb!

11:11.045 --> 11:12.838
Remember those explosions in Incheon?

11:12.922 --> 11:15.007
The one back in oh-seven
and then in twenty twelve?

11:15.883 --> 11:19.011
They were also ammonium
nitrate. Same methodology.

11:19.095 --> 11:21.889
The other top brass who competed
with you were blown up by those, right?

11:22.973 --> 11:23.974
Just like that.

11:24.058 --> 11:26.811
And once again, the one who
stands to profit is you, not Mr. Lee.

11:26.894 --> 11:27.937
I'll admit that Mr. Lee

11:28.020 --> 11:30.022
Arranged those other
explosions to help me out.

11:31.232 --> 11:33.693
Laika made Mr. Lee a very popular guy.

11:33.776 --> 11:35.778
That's thanks to what I
did behind the scenes.

11:36.570 --> 11:38.739
You know how much my
marketing tactics earned him?

11:38.823 --> 11:39.907
I was worth the hassle.

11:41.826 --> 11:43.160
And now…

11:43.244 --> 11:44.787
He tried to kill me, just like that.

11:45.621 --> 11:46.831
You're sure he's at fault, yeah?

11:48.040 --> 11:48.958
Yeah.

11:50.084 --> 11:51.210
But this time is different.

11:54.130 --> 11:56.257
You see that Mr. Lee had his
master killed the other day?

11:57.341 --> 11:58.259
It was on the news.

11:59.009 --> 12:00.469
Ewoo Shipping's Chairman Lee.

12:01.887 --> 12:02.805
Surely you heard.

12:04.974 --> 12:05.850
Ah.

12:06.517 --> 12:09.228
The chairman of a major company
was the master of a drug ring.

12:10.813 --> 12:12.314
Saying… "master" makes it sound like

12:12.398 --> 12:13.399
It's a kung fu movie.

12:15.568 --> 12:16.485
Cuff her.

12:18.446 --> 12:19.864
Follow the white rabbit.

12:21.615 --> 12:22.742
The chairman was a pawn.

12:23.743 --> 12:24.994
He wasn't in charge.

12:26.203 --> 12:28.372
The chairman of a major corporation served
at the feet of a drug lord for more than

12:28.456 --> 12:30.624
a decade, only to be thrown away.

12:31.751 --> 12:32.877
Do you see what I'm saying?

12:35.671 --> 12:36.547
Mr. Lee…

12:37.923 --> 12:38.924
Is the devil.

12:41.343 --> 12:42.219
Hey!

12:42.303 --> 12:43.554
Found anything?

12:43.637 --> 12:44.555
Someone's here!

12:45.097 --> 12:46.515
Over there. Inside!

12:47.057 --> 12:48.476
- Hurry up!
- What is it?

12:48.559 --> 12:49.393
Wait up.

12:49.477 --> 12:50.936
Someone just found a survivor.

12:53.189 --> 12:54.106
I'll go check it out.

12:54.648 --> 12:55.775
Can you bring this guy to a doctor?

12:55.858 --> 12:56.734
Huh?

12:56.817 --> 12:58.068
Yes, sir.

12:58.152 --> 12:59.028
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three!

12:59.111 --> 13:00.613
- One, two, three!
- One, two, three! -One, two, three!

13:00.696 --> 13:03.699
One, two, three! One…

13:03.783 --> 13:04.700
Later this year,

13:04.784 --> 13:06.869
We're expanding into the Chinese market.

13:07.578 --> 13:09.038
I know you can't understand,

13:09.121 --> 13:10.873
But it would make us
as powerful as Samsung.

13:11.957 --> 13:13.751
In a critical time like this,

13:14.335 --> 13:16.003
Lee Hak-seung was butchered.

13:16.962 --> 13:18.672
Half of HQ was obliterated.

13:23.844 --> 13:24.678
What does that sound like?

13:26.138 --> 13:27.223
Lee you know,

13:27.848 --> 13:29.475
Has plans to clean house.

13:30.059 --> 13:31.477
Well, he's sure ambitious, isn't he?

13:32.686 --> 13:33.521
So, who is he really?

13:34.063 --> 13:35.397
I have no idea.

13:35.481 --> 13:37.525
Oh… Yeah.

13:37.608 --> 13:38.526
- Sure.
- I came up with remote marketing

13:38.609 --> 13:40.027
tactics. That was the request of Mr. Lee.

13:41.153 --> 13:43.656
He never showed his face
to any of us. Not once.

13:43.739 --> 13:45.241
He controlled things like a ghost.

13:46.617 --> 13:47.701
The only person who saw him…

13:48.953 --> 13:50.037
Was Lee Hak-seung.

13:51.372 --> 13:52.706
Yeah.

13:52.790 --> 13:55.626
I have no clue whatsoever who Mr. Lee is.

13:56.293 --> 13:57.169
No smoking, Ma'am.

14:03.759 --> 14:05.094
That said, I do know his name.

14:08.097 --> 14:09.014
You wanna know?

14:13.102 --> 14:14.603
You finally look like you're interested.

14:17.064 --> 14:18.190
I'm so tired.

14:18.274 --> 14:19.900
You're fine cause you didn't talk.

14:19.984 --> 14:20.901
Let's break now?

14:21.569 --> 14:22.903
Hey, young man.

14:22.987 --> 14:24.238
Get me an order of haejang-guk.

14:24.864 --> 14:26.991
I'm diabetic, so it's
important. I can't skip meals.

14:28.325 --> 14:29.243
Ah!

14:29.326 --> 14:30.578
Yes,

14:30.661 --> 14:32.538
I told my driver to come
here, since he also survived.

14:33.163 --> 14:34.206
If you see him,

14:34.290 --> 14:35.749
Tell him to go get my insulin.

14:37.751 --> 14:39.044
And since we're taking a break,

14:40.170 --> 14:41.213
Can we do this?

14:42.089 --> 14:44.383
Some charges prosecution filed against me.

14:45.384 --> 14:46.552
Let's get those dismissed, yeah?

14:47.636 --> 14:48.554
Hmm?

14:52.600 --> 14:53.475
The survivor

14:53.559 --> 14:54.435
Is named Seo Young-rak.

14:55.019 --> 14:55.895
He's twenty eight years old

14:56.562 --> 14:58.230
I guess he was living inside the factory.

14:59.023 --> 15:00.774
The factory's entire ceiling collapsed,

15:00.858 --> 15:02.735
But he wasn't near the
fire so he survived.

15:03.777 --> 15:06.030
There was a female factory
worker among the deceased.

15:06.113 --> 15:07.031
He's her son.

15:07.948 --> 15:09.074
Her name was

15:09.158 --> 15:10.409
Yook Pil-soon, fifty-six.

15:10.492 --> 15:13.245
She's been living there ever since
the whole place was a greenhouse.

15:13.329 --> 15:16.415
When Mr. Lee bought the building
and turned it into a drug factory,

15:16.498 --> 15:17.958
She still stuck around the place

15:18.042 --> 15:19.543
And did menial work.

15:19.627 --> 15:20.836
Her son is the only survivor?

15:21.420 --> 15:23.088
Yes, no one else made it out.

15:23.172 --> 15:25.633
We're still searching the
back of the second floor,

15:25.716 --> 15:27.176
But it's unlikely we'll find anyone.

15:28.135 --> 15:30.054
But there was also a severely injured dog,

15:30.137 --> 15:30.971
Which we sent over

15:31.055 --> 15:32.181
For vet treatment.

15:45.486 --> 15:46.779
That woman is such a snake.

15:51.241 --> 15:53.118
Druggies look up to Mr. Lee

15:53.202 --> 15:54.411
Like he's Steve Jobs or something.

15:55.454 --> 15:56.580
She created that image of him, huh?

15:58.749 --> 16:01.043
Murder rumors have been
swirling about Lee Hak-seung.

16:01.835 --> 16:03.420
A heart attack doesn't seem to make
sense with his family and medical

16:03.504 --> 16:05.089
histories.

16:06.048 --> 16:07.174
You think Mr. Lee really did it?

16:08.217 --> 16:10.010
Well, if she's being
honest with us, then sure.

16:11.470 --> 16:13.263
Or she could be fucking around with us.

16:13.806 --> 16:16.058
Either way, look into his
death and see what sticks.

16:16.141 --> 16:17.059
Yes, sir.

16:27.528 --> 16:28.445
Huh?

16:38.998 --> 16:40.833
How'd she get hypoglycemic shock?

16:41.667 --> 16:42.793
She ate and took her meds.

16:45.462 --> 16:47.089
The driver brought the meds, didn't he?

16:47.172 --> 16:48.465
Yes.

16:48.549 --> 16:49.717
Go find him.

16:49.800 --> 16:50.718
I'm on it now.

17:01.979 --> 17:03.480
I thought you said he had passed out.

17:03.564 --> 17:05.274
I spoke to the doctor for maybe, like,

17:05.357 --> 17:06.358
Three minutes?

17:06.442 --> 17:07.651
This guy just totally vanished.

17:08.318 --> 17:10.529
I was told it would still be
a while before he woke up.

17:11.196 --> 17:13.115
Get hospital security
and block all the exits.

17:14.283 --> 17:15.200
You can't lose this guy.

17:15.826 --> 17:16.702
He's the only one who survived.

17:20.205 --> 17:21.165
Wait.

17:21.248 --> 17:22.166
Can you rewind?

17:24.960 --> 17:27.421
RADIOLOGY EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

17:28.630 --> 17:30.716
Don't even bother going
back to the ER again.

17:31.300 --> 17:33.218
I doubt he'd go back to where he's been.

17:34.845 --> 17:37.222
He's going to try to find
some way out of the building.

17:37.306 --> 17:38.348
Ask the hospital

17:38.432 --> 17:40.434
To post guards at every restroom.

17:40.517 --> 17:42.519
I checked the hallways security footage,

17:43.854 --> 17:45.272
But the coverage stops beyond that point.

17:58.619 --> 18:00.662
Is there anywhere in the
hospital without security cams?

18:36.573 --> 18:38.367
Those belonged to his mom, Yook Pil-soon,

18:38.951 --> 18:40.119
But he won't look at them.

18:41.370 --> 18:42.663
He hasn't even said a single word yet.

18:43.330 --> 18:45.290
Seo Young-rak had both these
cell phones on his person.

18:46.166 --> 18:47.501
Someone just messaged one of them.

18:48.627 --> 18:49.711
It isn't spam, I don't think.

18:50.546 --> 18:51.755
It's in code.

18:51.839 --> 18:53.132
Was his drug test positive?

18:53.215 --> 18:54.133
No, negative.

19:01.682 --> 19:02.599
Seo Young-rak.

19:04.143 --> 19:05.018
I hear your mother

19:05.102 --> 19:06.019
Called you Rak, didn't she?

19:07.646 --> 19:08.856
You mind if I call you that?

19:09.857 --> 19:10.816
Who is Mr. Lee?

19:15.362 --> 19:16.280
I see.

19:17.823 --> 19:18.740
Though I assume…

19:19.491 --> 19:21.451
You'd know who's a level
or two higher than you.

19:25.164 --> 19:25.998
Committed to silence, huh?

19:27.791 --> 19:29.168
I was told you've kept
quiet this whole time.

19:29.251 --> 19:30.252
Who are you doing it for?

19:34.381 --> 19:37.259
I'm… aware, you grew up in that kinda org.

19:37.342 --> 19:39.052
It makes a man like you blindly loyal.

19:40.345 --> 19:41.471
To repay you,

19:41.555 --> 19:43.265
They murder your mom and almost kill you.

19:44.349 --> 19:47.269
All of that thanks to a boss
you've never even laid eyes on.

19:47.352 --> 19:48.395
Right?

19:48.478 --> 19:49.688
I feel bad for you, Rak.

19:50.981 --> 19:52.608
You're no different
from that dog, are you?

19:52.691 --> 19:53.609
Huh?

19:53.692 --> 19:54.568
One dog made it outta there.

19:54.651 --> 19:57.738
Even though his fur is matted with
blood, he still wags his tail at people.

19:58.947 --> 20:00.282
Is the dog okay?

20:03.076 --> 20:04.870
I can show you the dog

20:05.537 --> 20:06.413
Right here.

20:06.496 --> 20:07.372
Uh… Yeah, here's the picture.

20:07.456 --> 20:08.415
Bunch of heartless punks.

20:09.416 --> 20:11.752
As soon as we found the dog
we moved him to a hospital.

20:11.835 --> 20:12.711
Dong-woo,

20:12.794 --> 20:13.962
What happened to the dog?

20:14.046 --> 20:15.714
Yes, sir. Well…

20:15.797 --> 20:17.299
The dog's skin was
badly burned from the fire,

20:17.382 --> 20:18.926
So they can't operate yet.

20:19.009 --> 20:21.303
But they did what they could
and are keeping an eye on him.

20:21.386 --> 20:22.888
He's in a lot of pain, so

20:22.971 --> 20:25.682
They're giving him painkillers
and sedatives to keep him alive.

20:26.391 --> 20:27.309
'Kay.

20:28.727 --> 20:29.645
Let's go.

20:33.357 --> 20:36.026
BON ANIMAL MEDICAL CENTER

20:48.747 --> 20:49.665
What's the dog's name?

20:54.544 --> 20:55.462
Jindo Dog.

20:58.090 --> 20:58.924
He's no Jindo.

21:02.094 --> 21:03.136
His esophagus

21:03.220 --> 21:04.137
Was depressed.

21:04.221 --> 21:05.347
They said he should be
able to eat, though,

21:05.931 --> 21:07.683
Once they open up a passageway.

21:08.767 --> 21:10.143
Can't bark anymore, though.

21:13.188 --> 21:14.940
Was Mr. Lee really responsible for this?

21:16.066 --> 21:18.819
It closely matches his M.O. from
other times he's cleaned house.

21:19.611 --> 21:21.655
Someone gets on his
nerves, he wipes out everyone.

21:21.738 --> 21:22.990
Their families,

21:23.073 --> 21:24.366
Their dogs, and whatnot.

21:25.033 --> 21:25.951
Someone once said

21:27.327 --> 21:28.412
That Mr. Lee is the devil.

21:34.626 --> 21:35.544
Can you get him?

21:36.878 --> 21:37.796
I have to.

21:46.805 --> 21:47.723
How, though?

21:48.890 --> 21:52.019
No one alive knows where or
even who the hell Mr Lee is.

21:57.441 --> 21:58.400
I'll find him, though.

22:06.825 --> 22:10.162
There've been a few people over the years
who have each made claim to being Mr. Lee.

22:11.246 --> 22:13.040
They all spoke poorly of
each other, all suspicious.

22:14.708 --> 22:17.002
It wasn't unusual for them to
start fights at the factory.

22:17.919 --> 22:20.172
I had a co-worker lose
his hand in one once.

22:20.255 --> 22:21.256
I understand.

22:21.340 --> 22:23.383
He needed to clean house,
so he blew them all away.

22:24.551 --> 22:26.803
You and your dog woulda just
been collateral damage then.

22:26.887 --> 22:27.804
No, no.

22:27.888 --> 22:29.389
No one knew I was back there.

22:30.140 --> 22:31.016
I returned early

22:31.099 --> 22:32.559
From a business trip in China.

22:35.145 --> 22:36.188
Here you go.

22:36.271 --> 22:38.732
So, these are both your
burner phones, is that right?

22:39.316 --> 22:40.776
- One of them's for work?
- There's a buyer from

22:40.859 --> 22:42.319
China who texts that cell.

22:43.487 --> 22:44.988
You speak to the Chinese buyer then?

22:45.530 --> 22:46.448
Yes.

22:50.535 --> 22:51.370
It's an ASCII code.

22:51.995 --> 22:53.955
Eight p.m. tomorrow, Acre Hotel Suite.

22:55.999 --> 22:58.293
I was supposed to bring the
chinese buyer to Mr Park.

23:03.673 --> 23:05.467
Meaning, this is about Mr. Lee's expansion

23:06.510 --> 23:08.345
- Into China?
- Yeah.

23:09.721 --> 23:11.390
Sounds like Mr. Lee
won't be there, though.

23:12.224 --> 23:13.141
Not quite.

23:13.934 --> 23:15.394
The buyer's one condition is

23:15.477 --> 23:17.062
Mr. Lee has to be there for the deal.

23:18.897 --> 23:21.441
The buyer’s also the top
manufactuer of an ingredient we need.

23:21.983 --> 23:24.820
We need him to sell us that
ingredient or there's no deal.

23:24.903 --> 23:27.906
We'll take his stuff, make our drugs, and
we'll come back with the finished product

23:28.490 --> 23:30.117
And finalize the deal with him.

23:30.200 --> 23:32.411
Mr. Lee will make an
appearance when it's done, I see.

23:34.454 --> 23:35.664
Does your office know you're back yet?

23:36.331 --> 23:37.624
No, not yet.

23:37.707 --> 23:38.625
Okay then,

23:40.001 --> 23:41.294
Let's tell them you're still in China,

23:41.920 --> 23:44.172
And that the buyer still
hasn't contacted you yet.

23:45.966 --> 23:47.050
Yeah…

23:47.134 --> 23:48.385
We have eighteen hours, team.

23:48.468 --> 23:49.386
Go brush your teeth.

23:50.053 --> 23:50.971
It's all-nighter time.

24:01.231 --> 24:02.149
Look at me.

24:20.250 --> 24:21.877
MR. LEE

24:32.512 --> 24:33.597
Buyer, Jin Ha-rim.

24:34.764 --> 24:35.974
He's Chinese,

24:36.057 --> 24:37.642
But he's from Mokpo, South Jeolla.

24:38.477 --> 24:40.020
He's from Korea, so
that's what he goes by.

24:40.979 --> 24:44.483
Jilin has quickly become the largest
drug market in all of China as of late.

24:44.566 --> 24:46.151
The true market size is unknown.

24:46.818 --> 24:48.778
Word on the street is
that half the cash is his

24:48.862 --> 24:51.072
In the Jilin drug market these days.

24:51.156 --> 24:52.824
He makes hundreds of millions every year.

24:53.408 --> 24:54.326
It's untraceable, though.

24:55.494 --> 24:57.078
He's obsessed with not
leaving a paper trail.

24:57.871 --> 24:58.788
Ever.

25:02.584 --> 25:03.835
But out of nowhere,

25:03.919 --> 25:05.295
Mr. Lee sent him a sample,

25:06.046 --> 25:07.047
Asking if he was interested in a deal.

25:09.341 --> 25:11.343
I think Jin was pretty shocked

25:11.426 --> 25:13.178
That Mr. Lee even knew about him.

25:16.264 --> 25:17.557
Jin responded immediately:

25:18.975 --> 25:19.976
"I'm going to Seoul

25:20.727 --> 25:21.603
To see you, Mr. Lee."

25:23.271 --> 25:25.065
Park Sun-Chang is set to welcome Jin.

25:25.148 --> 25:26.483
He's one of Laika's founding members.

25:27.108 --> 25:28.944
Each of those times Mr. Lee cleaned house,

25:29.027 --> 25:31.404
Gritty Park found some way
to come out the other side.

25:31.488 --> 25:34.449
He used to be the director of
international affairs at Hankuk Air.

25:34.533 --> 25:36.201
He's a man from the corporate world he
was known to take care of business pretty

25:36.284 --> 25:37.953
well.

25:38.662 --> 25:40.747
At the factory last year, there
was a fight over labor rights.

25:41.373 --> 25:43.166
Park proved his place In the organization

25:43.917 --> 25:45.126
With every swing of his knife.

25:45.877 --> 25:47.087
I take it that

25:47.170 --> 25:48.922
There's no way Park
knows what Jin looks like?

25:49.005 --> 25:51.049
Yeah, only a handful of
people have actually met Jin.

25:51.591 --> 25:53.093
And Jin has never seen Park before either?

25:53.176 --> 25:54.886
I'm supposed to
introduce the two of them today.

26:05.480 --> 26:07.190
Tell Park the meetings
been pushed an hour.

26:08.483 --> 26:09.401
Same place still.

26:10.110 --> 26:11.361
We'll meet Jin at eight as scheduled.

26:13.363 --> 26:14.614
We will direct this deal.

26:16.116 --> 26:17.033
Our way!

26:20.870 --> 26:21.788
We'll meet Jin first.

26:56.615 --> 26:57.532
They made it here.

27:09.044 --> 27:10.170
I said, they changed 'em all.

27:10.253 --> 27:11.129
- Did you
- Outta my way.

27:11.212 --> 27:12.130
Leave some out?

27:19.220 --> 27:20.138
Hello, Mr. Jin.

27:24.184 --> 27:25.435
It's nice to meet you.
I'm Park Sun-chang, hi.

27:28.730 --> 27:29.648
It's an honor.

27:54.381 --> 27:55.256
Alright.

27:55.340 --> 27:56.174
We'll wait for you in the other room, sir.

28:24.828 --> 28:25.745
There he is.

28:39.592 --> 28:40.510
And who are you?

28:41.302 --> 28:42.512
Sir. Just the…

28:42.595 --> 28:43.513
One you're supposed to meet…

28:45.849 --> 28:46.933
Are you Mr. Lee?

28:49.018 --> 28:49.936
I am not.

28:50.520 --> 28:51.438
Sir, I'm-

28:54.441 --> 28:56.025
I came here to see Mr. Lee.

28:58.111 --> 28:59.446
Once we get your very fine materials

29:00.113 --> 29:01.364
And make a batch of product,

29:01.448 --> 29:03.032
Mr. Lee will give you the goods himself.

29:14.669 --> 29:15.587
Thank you sir.

29:17.297 --> 29:19.466
Our company has a
complex hierarchical system.

29:23.970 --> 29:26.681
Do you understand what it
means, me coming here to Seoul, huh?

29:30.435 --> 29:32.103
I do not travel, ever.

29:33.730 --> 29:34.898
I don't leave my house.

29:36.983 --> 29:38.109
Things outside my home

29:38.193 --> 29:40.195
Seem to always have a
way of pissing me off.

29:43.031 --> 29:44.449
You know what irritates me the most?

29:47.702 --> 29:48.620
LED light bulbs.

29:50.079 --> 29:50.997
They're so loud.

29:52.665 --> 29:53.583
They hurt my head.

30:02.509 --> 30:04.052
And yet, I flew here to Seoul.

30:05.720 --> 30:06.888
Where is Mr. Lee?

30:17.816 --> 30:19.901
Fuck you. How dare you do this to me?

30:19.984 --> 30:21.152
Who

30:21.236 --> 30:22.153
The hell are you?

30:23.112 --> 30:25.240
Lee Min-ho sat next to me at the show!

30:25.323 --> 30:26.658
Yeah?

30:26.741 --> 30:27.659
Did you guys get a pic?

30:28.368 --> 30:29.536
Y'see?

30:29.619 --> 30:30.745
He has the smallest head I've ever seen!

30:31.996 --> 30:33.665
The little bell is so excited!

30:36.709 --> 30:37.544
I got them tickets to a

30:37.627 --> 30:39.254
Fashion show the actor
Lee Min-ho attended.

30:39.838 --> 30:41.130
So they made the effort to come

30:41.214 --> 30:42.882
Earlier than we originally planned.

30:42.966 --> 30:44.759
- Oh.
- What do you mean, effort?

30:44.843 --> 30:47.679
When else would I ever get the
chance to sit by Lee Min-Ho?

30:53.226 --> 30:54.143
Here you go.

30:56.104 --> 30:57.313
Your gift.

30:57.397 --> 30:58.481
Hey, hey,

30:58.565 --> 31:00.275
I'm blocked. Hey.

31:00.358 --> 31:01.276
Handsome, yeah?

31:02.944 --> 31:03.862
Oh, it's-

31:03.945 --> 31:05.321
I don't know how to tie a tie.

31:05.405 --> 31:06.489
I'll watch a how-to video.

31:08.491 --> 31:09.409
Let me teach you.

31:13.454 --> 31:14.372
Madam!

31:18.209 --> 31:19.085
That woman is…

31:19.168 --> 31:20.545
Exceptionally lovely.

31:20.628 --> 31:21.588
She has the

31:21.671 --> 31:23.047
The face and style of an actress, with the

31:23.131 --> 31:24.048
Body of a model.

31:24.883 --> 31:26.175
Mr. Jin,

31:26.259 --> 31:27.510
Have you ever heard
the old Chinese proverb,

31:27.594 --> 31:29.012
- The one about how good deeds-
- Shit.

31:31.723 --> 31:32.640
Hmm.

31:33.433 --> 31:35.059
Models have itty bitty tits.

31:37.562 --> 31:38.605
Are these tiny?

31:44.193 --> 31:45.111
Hey, honey…

31:52.327 --> 31:53.244
This is fake?

31:54.704 --> 31:55.997
One of our suppliers has this
brother-in-law in Hangzhou who makes

31:56.080 --> 31:57.665
these.

31:57.749 --> 31:59.834
Let me know if you'd like it
and i'll let him know to send one

31:59.918 --> 32:01.711
He also does custom watches if you're-

32:02.378 --> 32:03.212
Honey.

32:06.299 --> 32:07.800
Spending is the only thing that I can do.

32:08.509 --> 32:09.552
Little bell!

32:11.596 --> 32:12.513
Yeah?

32:13.848 --> 32:14.766
Attention.

32:16.768 --> 32:17.685
Turn about.

32:34.494 --> 32:36.537
Why buy all this fake shit?

32:47.966 --> 32:48.883
Just knowing

32:49.509 --> 32:51.761
That you now know what
i actually look like,

32:55.598 --> 32:56.516
Just that fact…

33:00.103 --> 33:02.063
It's enough for me to feed
this boy to the dogs of Jilin.

33:05.108 --> 33:06.901
But he knows his place pretty damn well.

33:08.027 --> 33:08.945
I like this guy.

33:09.487 --> 33:11.280
Hmm? This is what

33:11.906 --> 33:13.116
All staff should be like, Eh?

33:14.117 --> 33:15.034
Thanks.

33:22.917 --> 33:24.919
"The happy medium is the way to go."

33:28.673 --> 33:29.799
That's a saying

33:29.882 --> 33:32.927
You Koreans invented. Uh…

33:35.513 --> 33:37.348
Yet you people are always extreme.

33:39.267 --> 33:40.560
You run cold

33:40.643 --> 33:41.769
Or way too hot.

33:43.187 --> 33:44.439
You're all a mess, you know that?

33:45.940 --> 33:48.067
I need Lee!

33:52.530 --> 33:54.032
That Lee's a funny guy!

33:55.324 --> 33:57.201
"Here's a sample for you.

33:57.285 --> 33:59.537
Hope we can work together some day."

34:04.333 --> 34:05.251
You know…

34:06.794 --> 34:07.920
Even when people know me,

34:09.797 --> 34:10.965
They act like they don't,

34:11.549 --> 34:13.092
Because they wanna keep breathing.

34:14.093 --> 34:15.887
Hey? You bastards, though…

34:57.637 --> 34:58.554
I could choose…

34:59.931 --> 35:02.558
To knock you both off right
now and I would lose nothing.

35:04.894 --> 35:05.895
Actually…

35:05.978 --> 35:08.064
Two days ago, we… had a fire to deal with.

35:08.856 --> 35:09.857
Factory fires are chaotic.

35:10.858 --> 35:12.235
Things have been hectic, but we wanted

35:12.318 --> 35:13.236
To make this deal

35:13.319 --> 35:14.237
Still go smoothly.

35:15.571 --> 35:16.489
I promise, next time…

35:17.115 --> 35:19.033
Mr. Lee will be at the meeting, sir.

35:19.117 --> 35:20.451
Once again,

35:20.535 --> 35:21.577
Apologies for his absence.

35:22.203 --> 35:23.287
This time,

35:23.371 --> 35:24.455
We brought you

35:24.539 --> 35:25.957
A special sample of our favorite product.

35:27.542 --> 35:28.751
What we showed you previously

35:28.835 --> 35:29.919
Was our Voyager series.

35:30.002 --> 35:30.920
This is

35:31.003 --> 35:32.130
Our first big hit,

35:33.047 --> 35:34.090
Its Laika sir

35:34.173 --> 35:36.300
If the Voyager is trendy and sensual,

35:36.384 --> 35:37.510
Laika

35:37.593 --> 35:38.886
Is classic

35:38.970 --> 35:39.887
Substantial.

36:37.653 --> 36:38.571
Tell me, how is it?

36:40.114 --> 36:41.032
What?

37:04.430 --> 37:05.348
Mr. Jin.

37:05.973 --> 37:06.933
How do you

37:07.016 --> 37:08.059
Prefer we collect your materials?

37:10.978 --> 37:11.896
Shit.

37:26.911 --> 37:27.828
Do you think

37:28.704 --> 37:31.832
I'm actually in the mood to
seal a deal with you assholes?

37:31.916 --> 37:33.292
Sorry, sir, but the gun is well…

37:34.502 --> 37:36.504
I'm just a simple employee on the payroll.

37:37.588 --> 37:38.464
I report to

37:38.547 --> 37:39.590
And take orders from the top.

37:44.929 --> 37:46.430
We'll be in touch with you.

37:49.475 --> 37:50.393
One of two things:

37:52.311 --> 37:54.188
I'll either give you the
ingredients right then,

37:56.440 --> 37:58.067
Or I'll just slaughter all of you.

38:02.488 --> 38:03.406
But either way,

38:04.031 --> 38:05.157
You just wait for Jin.

38:19.130 --> 38:20.464
Hurry or we'll miss it.

38:20.548 --> 38:21.590
You go in front.

38:21.674 --> 38:22.591
Run.

38:29.140 --> 38:30.266
Sir, we've checked the monitors.

38:30.349 --> 38:31.225
It should all be fine now.

38:43.529 --> 38:44.447
Were you scared?

38:47.950 --> 38:50.161
"Enough for me to feed this
boy to the dogs of Jilin."

38:50.244 --> 38:51.662
"To feed the boy to the dogs of Jilin."

38:51.746 --> 38:52.621
"Enough for me to…"

38:52.705 --> 38:53.998
"Enough for me to feed this boy to the

38:54.081 --> 38:54.957
Dogs of Jilin."

39:00.212 --> 39:01.464
Okay, get in position.

39:04.008 --> 39:05.051
It's Minute Fifty-seven.

39:05.134 --> 39:06.052
Three more minutes to go.

39:13.559 --> 39:16.562
"Even when people know me, they
act like they don't, because…"

39:16.645 --> 39:17.563
'Kay.

39:28.240 --> 39:29.408
Yeah…

39:29.492 --> 39:30.409
That's our guy.

39:35.539 --> 39:36.874
I assume you heard about Incheon?

39:38.959 --> 39:40.878
I feel bad for your mom and all that.

39:42.713 --> 39:44.256
But dozens of lives depend on this deal.

39:46.008 --> 39:47.635
So, is the salt factory ready yet?

39:47.718 --> 39:48.636
Huh?

39:51.764 --> 39:52.681
Shithead.

39:54.225 --> 39:55.142
Come on, kid.

39:59.897 --> 40:01.482
"Happy medium is the
way to go. You Koreans."

40:02.608 --> 40:04.693
'Kay, set-up team, Gotta hurry it up.

40:04.777 --> 40:05.736
Dong-woo,

40:05.820 --> 40:06.821
Get out of there.

40:06.904 --> 40:07.822
I'm almost done here.

40:08.739 --> 40:09.657
Elevator is open.

40:09.740 --> 40:10.658
Making approach.

40:11.992 --> 40:12.910
Dong-woo, we're out of time.

40:12.993 --> 40:14.203
- Get outta there.
- Kay

40:14.286 --> 40:14.954
Leaving now, sir.

40:16.455 --> 40:17.540
Oh!

40:17.623 --> 40:19.458
Wait, wait, wait, wait! Hold on.

40:21.043 --> 40:21.919
They turned, almost there.

40:22.002 --> 40:23.295
Dong-woo, you have to hide somewhere.

40:23.379 --> 40:24.296
Sit tight.

40:26.090 --> 40:27.091
Here we go.

40:27.174 --> 40:28.300
Ten meters.

40:28.384 --> 40:29.468
Support team,

40:29.552 --> 40:30.469
Remain calm. Be ready.

40:31.262 --> 40:32.471
Dong-woo, did you hide?

40:32.555 --> 40:33.431
Dong-woo.

40:33.514 --> 40:35.099
- Dong-woo?
- Sir, help me.

40:36.350 --> 40:37.435
What do I do?

40:37.518 --> 40:39.895
- Where should I hide?
- You idiot. Just hide anywhere!

40:41.939 --> 40:42.857
Good evening.

40:44.108 --> 40:45.025
Support team,

40:45.109 --> 40:46.402
Just trust me and

40:46.485 --> 40:47.403
Let's go.

41:20.352 --> 41:21.729
A pleasure to meet you here sir.

41:30.029 --> 41:30.905
Im Park Sun-Chang.

41:32.698 --> 41:33.616
Don't smile.

41:41.415 --> 41:42.708
Don't bother smiling or bowing,

41:42.791 --> 41:44.293
Just to get on my good side.

41:45.586 --> 41:46.962
Doesn't matter, I'm not gonna like you.

41:49.590 --> 41:50.799
Uh, Sir?

41:50.883 --> 41:51.884
We will wait for you over there, Mr. Jin.

42:11.445 --> 42:12.404
I need Lee!

42:14.198 --> 42:15.950
Wow… you bastards crack me up.

42:17.326 --> 42:19.328
You called me first, to
set this whole thing up,

42:19.411 --> 42:20.329
Huh?

42:24.875 --> 42:25.793
So, where's your leader?

42:27.169 --> 42:29.213
Well, I'm supposed to
welcome you here first

42:29.296 --> 42:30.172
Tonight in Seoul.

42:30.256 --> 42:31.549
- Later on, Mr. Lee will-
- You know…

42:33.592 --> 42:34.760
Even those who uh

42:35.719 --> 42:38.097
Who know me, pretend
that they don't know me

42:38.180 --> 42:39.348
Because they want to keep breathing.

42:40.766 --> 42:42.059
Just knowing that you

42:42.142 --> 42:45.229
Know what I look like is
enough to wipe you off this Earth.

42:48.816 --> 42:49.858
You know if I wanted to,

42:49.942 --> 42:51.986
I could choose to knock you
both off. I'd lose nothing.

42:52.945 --> 42:53.862
You see?

42:54.655 --> 42:55.573
Sure.

42:56.448 --> 42:57.366
Now drink.

43:06.458 --> 43:07.960
I gotta say, I like your friend, Seo.

43:09.628 --> 43:11.130
He knows his place damn well.

43:11.213 --> 43:12.840
This is what the staff should be like.

43:20.097 --> 43:20.973
Now…

43:21.056 --> 43:21.974
Let's begin.

43:24.977 --> 43:27.021
First off, you'll never
have to worry about security.

43:28.314 --> 43:29.148
Inside our organization,

43:30.190 --> 43:32.234
Only two or three
people above and below us

43:32.318 --> 43:33.819
Even know about this deal.

43:34.820 --> 43:36.113
So, we have very secure operations.

43:38.240 --> 43:40.159
The sample we showed you
before was called Voyager.

43:40.701 --> 43:42.077
This is our bestseller,

43:42.161 --> 43:43.078
Laika.

43:44.913 --> 43:45.831
Hold on.

43:49.126 --> 43:50.836
What did you add to it
to make it so opaque?

43:54.173 --> 43:55.090
Is this Laika?

44:00.054 --> 44:00.971
Oh, shit.

44:01.513 --> 44:02.431
Sorry.

44:06.143 --> 44:07.394
Are you okay?

44:07.478 --> 44:08.937
Oh… I'm so damn clumsy.

44:10.564 --> 44:11.857
Oh, no, no, no.

44:11.940 --> 44:12.858
Everything's fine, ma'am.

44:14.735 --> 44:15.611
I'll take care of this.

44:18.864 --> 44:19.782
Mr. Jin.

44:22.826 --> 44:24.370
I'll prepare the lines for you, huh?

44:34.588 --> 44:36.882
I hand-selected the materials for
this, so it's the highest purity.

44:41.470 --> 44:42.388
Also,

44:43.639 --> 44:45.307
I've brought you
something even more special.

44:51.689 --> 44:53.023
This is a new, stronger stimulant.

44:53.774 --> 44:55.901
Specially made just
for the Chinese market.

45:00.155 --> 45:01.073
Sir, please.

45:03.158 --> 45:04.535
Let's focus on Laika for him today?

45:05.536 --> 45:06.995
I haven't briefed him
on our new product yet.

45:09.873 --> 45:10.791
Let go.

45:14.920 --> 45:15.963
Can't we stay with the plan?

45:18.340 --> 45:20.050
Have you completely lost your mind?

45:27.599 --> 45:28.517
Hit me.

45:29.893 --> 45:30.811
Sure thing.

45:40.863 --> 45:42.614
May I recommend that
you start with this one?

46:18.192 --> 46:19.109
How's it feel?

46:27.367 --> 46:28.202
Tell me, bastard:

46:28.744 --> 46:30.037
Are you Mr. Lee?

46:31.747 --> 46:33.499
I promise he'll be here next time.

46:33.582 --> 46:35.542
- I swear, Mr. Jin.
- He better be there.

46:47.387 --> 46:50.724
Didn't I fucking say I only came
out to Seoul to see Mr. Lee today?

46:51.850 --> 46:52.810
If Mr. Lee

46:53.685 --> 46:54.812
Isn't here next time,

46:57.064 --> 46:58.482
You'll be the first one I chop to bits.

47:33.851 --> 47:35.561
Breathe, sir. Breathe!

47:35.644 --> 47:36.562
Sir, please.

47:37.855 --> 47:38.772
Stay awake.

47:39.690 --> 47:40.607
Captain Jo.

47:48.073 --> 47:49.783
I shouldn't have
crossed the line in there.

47:49.867 --> 47:50.784
I'm sorry, sir.

47:54.788 --> 47:55.706
Listen.

47:57.332 --> 47:59.042
If you fuck up this deal, then I'll- Shit.

48:18.979 --> 48:19.897
Hey!

48:19.980 --> 48:21.148
Is this all the ice they have?

48:21.231 --> 48:22.774
- Bring all the ice you can, come on!
- Sir.

48:22.858 --> 48:23.775
Yeah, run all of that ice in here!

48:23.859 --> 48:24.776
Hurry up!

48:25.694 --> 48:26.570
Pour, pour, pour, pour, pour.

48:49.343 --> 48:51.345
- No!
- Why me?!

48:52.054 --> 48:52.971
- Shh-Soo-jung!
- Why me?

48:53.055 --> 48:53.931
No!

48:54.014 --> 48:55.933
Why?!

49:00.520 --> 49:01.438
He needs air.

49:44.272 --> 49:45.190
You okay?

49:46.066 --> 49:46.984
Damn you. Shit.

49:49.236 --> 49:51.363
Who told you to piss off Park like
that? Its not your call to make.

49:52.489 --> 49:53.740
Are you wrong in the head?

49:53.824 --> 49:55.242
You think we're a team now do ya?

49:55.325 --> 49:56.535
Captain Jo, we-

49:56.618 --> 49:57.828
You do what I tell you to do,

49:57.911 --> 49:58.787
Whether you

49:58.870 --> 50:00.163
Want to or not.

50:00.247 --> 50:01.164
Maybe you…

50:04.334 --> 50:05.168
Just had a nightmare.

50:12.884 --> 50:14.052
Don't get clever with me.

50:15.512 --> 50:16.972
Without me, you can't do anything.

50:21.643 --> 50:22.561
Get smart.

50:23.687 --> 50:24.563
Don't you forget…

50:25.856 --> 50:27.190
I can lock you up anytime.

50:55.802 --> 50:57.054
Jin Ha-rim sent the burner a text.

50:58.472 --> 50:59.431
He wants to

50:59.514 --> 51:00.432
Go through with the deal.

51:01.016 --> 51:02.350
He says the ingredients are prepared.

51:06.063 --> 51:07.272
Motherfucker!

51:07.355 --> 51:09.483
Did you fuck that girl last night?

51:09.566 --> 51:10.692
Was she good?

51:10.776 --> 51:12.152
Where's the good hostess bar?

51:13.528 --> 51:14.905
Yeah, let's go find some tens!

51:15.781 --> 51:17.949
Okay! Lets do it!

51:18.825 --> 51:19.743
Thank you.

51:24.372 --> 51:25.749
Where will you cook the drugs?

51:27.084 --> 51:28.043
The factory burned down.

51:30.837 --> 51:32.297
There's a salt factory in Taean.

51:34.216 --> 51:35.801
Their product's second to none.

51:36.968 --> 51:38.386
There's two technicians there.

51:38.470 --> 51:39.304
They're geniuses.

51:40.639 --> 51:43.308
The only problem is, they were
born unable to hear or speak.

51:43.892 --> 51:45.727
After an accident last year,

51:45.811 --> 51:47.270
They set up the factory on their own.

51:49.439 --> 51:50.732
They don't work for us anymore.

51:50.816 --> 51:51.942
They're…

51:52.025 --> 51:52.943
Independent.

51:53.860 --> 51:55.028
I'm the only one they interact with.

51:56.238 --> 51:57.197
Only you? How come?

51:59.282 --> 52:00.492
Only I know their language.

52:14.131 --> 52:15.048
Hey, Captain.

52:15.590 --> 52:16.508
Come here.

52:22.055 --> 52:23.265
Ah, im alright don't worry.

52:26.393 --> 52:27.310
I gotta go inside.

52:34.401 --> 52:35.318
Hey.

52:36.611 --> 52:37.612
This is our interpreter.

52:38.238 --> 52:39.322
Nice to meet you.

52:39.406 --> 52:40.282
And you, too.

52:40.365 --> 52:41.032
I'm Jo Won-ho.

52:41.116 --> 52:41.575
Hi,

52:41.658 --> 52:42.159
I'm Kim Soo-hee.

52:43.493 --> 52:44.536
- The monitors are ready.
- Mmm.

52:50.625 --> 52:52.210
Hey.

52:55.505 --> 52:56.381
You're looking

52:56.464 --> 52:57.549
Even more handsome these days.

52:57.632 --> 52:59.092
The… Fuck?

52:59.176 --> 53:00.093
Translate it all, please.

53:00.177 --> 53:01.261
So fuckin' ugly!

53:01.970 --> 53:04.222
He looks he should be on
TV. No, no, no, no, no.

53:04.306 --> 53:05.849
What the hell? What do
you keep saying "no" for?

53:05.932 --> 53:07.225
What, what?

53:07.309 --> 53:09.436
Quiet! Quiet, quiet, quiet!

53:09.519 --> 53:10.520
Yo, yo, yo, yo.

53:12.022 --> 53:14.524
We got… this truck full of
stuff from a Chinese guy.

53:14.608 --> 53:15.609
What? A Chinese guy?

53:16.776 --> 53:17.736
Your eyes will

53:17.819 --> 53:19.237
Explode, it's so much. Okay, okay.

53:19.321 --> 53:20.030
Let's see it.

53:25.160 --> 53:26.036
Well, damn!

53:26.119 --> 53:27.078
One, two, two, three, four, five, six.

53:30.498 --> 53:31.666
Damn.

53:31.750 --> 53:32.667
How many are there?

53:33.293 --> 53:34.294
In two days?

53:34.377 --> 53:35.378
No way, no way, no way.

53:35.462 --> 53:36.588
Two days? Two days?

53:36.671 --> 53:38.215
No, no, Okay. We can do it.

53:38.298 --> 53:40.884
You crazy bastard, you came
out here to work us to death!

53:40.967 --> 53:42.969
You wanna suck up all our energy?

53:43.053 --> 53:44.763
I'm sucking you totally dry.

53:44.846 --> 53:47.390
- Suck and suck til you're empty.
- What is this, a coffee date?

53:47.474 --> 53:49.476
- Continue.
- Fuck you.

53:49.559 --> 53:50.685
No, fuck you.

53:50.769 --> 53:51.770
I did.

53:51.853 --> 53:52.771
Fuck you!

53:53.396 --> 53:54.564
Yo!

53:54.648 --> 53:55.565
Haul these inside.

53:56.316 --> 53:57.525
Go wash your hands. I'll make you dinner.

53:59.361 --> 54:01.363
Hey! You hungry?

54:01.446 --> 54:02.364
Let's eat real quick.

54:36.064 --> 54:37.857
What's wrong? You're sad.

54:39.442 --> 54:40.485
There was a big

54:40.568 --> 54:43.238
Explosion at the Incheon factory.

54:43.321 --> 54:44.239
My mother died.

54:44.781 --> 54:45.824
We couldn't

54:45.907 --> 54:47.993
Even hold a real funeral for her.

54:48.660 --> 54:49.577
The cops kept

54:50.370 --> 54:51.204
Swarming around.

54:53.039 --> 54:54.374
Your mother passed away?

54:55.417 --> 54:56.459
Which way's north?

54:56.543 --> 54:57.711
Go grab Some fish.

54:58.295 --> 55:00.046
Get some Croaker.

55:03.049 --> 55:04.259
His mother always

55:04.342 --> 55:05.593
Loved fish.

55:05.677 --> 55:07.345
You're right. Quickly.

55:13.727 --> 55:15.770
IN MEMORY OF YOOK PIL-SOON

55:21.234 --> 55:22.235
When our father

55:22.319 --> 55:23.737
Passed away,

55:23.820 --> 55:24.863
His mother did

55:24.946 --> 55:26.156
The same for us.

55:26.239 --> 55:28.033
That's right. I remember.

55:28.116 --> 55:29.826
Death means being without a body.

55:29.909 --> 55:30.827
So, I'm sure

55:31.536 --> 55:32.579
She'll come find us here.

55:58.938 --> 56:02.525
YOOK PIL-SOON

56:05.653 --> 56:06.988
Hmm. Mmm.

56:58.248 --> 56:59.332
Mmm.

56:59.416 --> 57:00.333
Hmm.

57:29.362 --> 57:30.280
Oh!

57:31.948 --> 57:32.949
Are they freaking robots?

57:33.032 --> 57:35.285
How can they work for
thirty straight hours?

57:35.368 --> 57:36.661
They've got drugs powering them.

57:36.744 --> 57:37.745
We just have coffee.

57:37.829 --> 57:39.372
- We're back.
- We're back with food!

57:39.456 --> 57:40.540
Finally!

57:40.623 --> 57:41.666
It seems Oh Yeon-ok will be

57:41.749 --> 57:43.168
Scapegoated for the factory explosion.

57:43.710 --> 57:44.669
Yeon-ok Paint, they say,

57:44.752 --> 57:45.628
Keeps producing more

57:45.712 --> 57:46.796
Decisive evidence.

57:46.880 --> 57:48.965
It's complicated because
she left things messy.

57:49.632 --> 57:51.676
Her autopsy results came in too.

57:51.759 --> 57:54.554
Hypoglycemic shock caused by a
hypertensive drug, not an inhibitor.

57:55.388 --> 57:56.848
Someone switched the meds,

57:56.931 --> 57:58.183
But we have nothing on the driver.

57:58.266 --> 57:59.184
He's not clever enough,

57:59.767 --> 58:01.478
Plus he passed the lie detector test.

58:01.561 --> 58:02.854
Mr. Lee punished her, it seems.

58:03.438 --> 58:04.355
Uh, Captain Jo…

58:05.064 --> 58:06.232
Here is

58:06.316 --> 58:07.734
Seo Young-rak's file. Take a look.

58:41.893 --> 58:42.977
This is from the wreckage.

58:44.687 --> 58:45.605
Who's this?

58:47.440 --> 58:48.358
That's not me.

58:49.651 --> 58:51.152
No, it obviously isn't.

58:51.236 --> 58:52.153
Who are you?

58:55.323 --> 58:56.157
I am myself.

58:57.367 --> 58:58.284
You fucking idiot.

58:59.827 --> 59:00.912
Can you give me a cigarette?

59:23.142 --> 59:25.895
Every month, Yook Pil-soon received
a shipping container full of bananas

59:25.979 --> 59:26.854
From Hong Kong.

59:27.772 --> 59:29.983
Along with the bananas,
the container usually had

59:30.066 --> 59:31.109
A kilo and a half of meth.

59:31.776 --> 59:32.986
But one time, she found a boy.

59:36.072 --> 59:37.240
I was eight years old.

59:39.617 --> 59:40.868
The four-year-old in the picture,

59:40.952 --> 59:42.161
Her son Young-rak,

59:42.245 --> 59:44.080
Was killed by a truck
unloading at the factory.

59:46.082 --> 59:47.458
They buried him without reporting it.

59:49.335 --> 59:52.297
So, I wore Young-rak's
clothes and I ate Young-rak's food.

59:55.174 --> 59:57.552
And I went to school
in the dead boy's name.

59:57.635 --> 59:58.845
It says his name

59:58.928 --> 01:00:00.221
On my National ID Card.

01:00:01.806 --> 01:00:02.724
Doesn't that mean…

01:00:04.058 --> 01:00:05.852
I'm now Seo Young-rak, am I not?

01:00:19.949 --> 01:00:20.867
Were you expecting anyone?

01:00:22.118 --> 01:00:23.244
Oh, no.

01:00:23.328 --> 01:00:24.245
No one should be here.

01:00:25.246 --> 01:00:26.372
Go back in and act normal.

01:00:27.206 --> 01:00:28.499
And don't forget:

01:00:28.583 --> 01:00:29.626
I am watching you.

01:00:29.709 --> 01:00:30.627
Go!

01:00:48.478 --> 01:00:49.812
The guy in front is Park Sun-chang.

01:00:51.189 --> 01:00:52.315
Then there are three cars.

01:00:53.274 --> 01:00:54.859
I can't make out the
license plate numbers.

01:00:57.445 --> 01:00:59.155
The men getting out
now look like security.

01:01:00.865 --> 01:01:02.116
Wait.

01:01:02.200 --> 01:01:03.368
Someone's sitting in the last car.

01:01:06.371 --> 01:01:07.830
Fuck me!

01:01:07.914 --> 01:01:08.873
It's loud as shit in here.

01:01:16.089 --> 01:01:17.507
Director Brian is here, waiting.

01:01:18.800 --> 01:01:19.717
What? Brian?

01:01:21.386 --> 01:01:22.303
"Director Brian is here."

01:01:22.929 --> 01:01:23.930
Park Sun-Chang called him "Director."

01:01:25.264 --> 01:01:26.182
Brian?

01:01:48.037 --> 01:01:48.955
Now, say hello.

01:01:49.497 --> 01:01:50.415
Brian, the director.

01:01:54.085 --> 01:01:55.044
We didn't have him on our list.

01:01:56.796 --> 01:01:58.464
Seo Young-rak, hello.

01:02:00.967 --> 01:02:02.176
You must be mad, aren't you?

01:02:02.760 --> 01:02:03.678
Huh?

01:02:04.345 --> 01:02:05.263
You're grief-stricken,

01:02:06.556 --> 01:02:07.473
Bitter

01:02:08.141 --> 01:02:09.100
And furious, right?

01:02:13.813 --> 01:02:16.232
I'm sure you feel awful. You
went through something tragic.

01:02:17.650 --> 01:02:18.484
I see you're in pain.

01:02:21.320 --> 01:02:23.114
I understand, and I'll ask a question:

01:02:23.197 --> 01:02:24.282
What is your faith, son?

01:02:25.992 --> 01:02:26.909
Tell him, Seo.

01:02:27.744 --> 01:02:28.578
No, it's alright.

01:02:29.412 --> 01:02:30.288
Let's start with

01:02:30.371 --> 01:02:32.165
The idea of faith and go from there.

01:02:32.248 --> 01:02:33.541
As the Holy Bible tells us,

01:02:34.667 --> 01:02:35.543
"When you ask,

01:02:35.626 --> 01:02:37.086
You must not doubt, but ask in faith."

01:02:47.180 --> 01:02:48.097
Now, of course…

01:02:49.557 --> 01:02:51.434
Your faith could be a little shaken up,

01:02:51.517 --> 01:02:52.685
But…

01:02:52.769 --> 01:02:53.770
My son, it's okay.

01:02:53.853 --> 01:02:55.396
I will help you find your center again.

01:03:04.071 --> 01:03:06.324
It's okay, you can rely on me now.

01:03:07.283 --> 01:03:08.201
Okay?

01:03:20.213 --> 01:03:21.589
Did Mr. Lee give that to you?

01:03:28.638 --> 01:03:29.722
He's heard of me then?

01:03:59.460 --> 01:04:00.378
Shit.

01:04:05.508 --> 01:04:06.425
Shit.

01:04:07.969 --> 01:04:08.886
Shit.

01:04:13.224 --> 01:04:14.475
How many times do I gotta warn you?

01:04:15.768 --> 01:04:17.144
Now keep your damn head down.

01:04:18.104 --> 01:04:19.939
Before I gouge your eyes out with a knife.

01:04:40.710 --> 01:04:41.961
Yes, sir.

01:04:42.044 --> 01:04:43.170
Let's chat.

01:04:43.254 --> 01:04:45.172
Seo Young-rak seems like an issue.

01:04:45.256 --> 01:04:47.091
Sincere apologies for his behavior.

01:04:47.633 --> 01:04:48.551
I taught him a

01:04:49.135 --> 01:04:50.678
lesson after you left
so he should understand-

01:04:50.761 --> 01:04:52.305
We no longer need Seo Young-rak.

01:04:53.097 --> 01:04:54.891
Let's continue without him.

01:04:54.974 --> 01:04:55.892
Sir, but the thing is…

01:04:57.059 --> 01:04:59.520
He's the one in charge of
all communications right now.

01:05:00.187 --> 01:05:02.273
- Couldn't we just-
- That wasn't a question, got it?

01:05:08.362 --> 01:05:09.405
Did you ID him?

01:05:09.488 --> 01:05:10.406
He got a file?

01:05:10.948 --> 01:05:11.824
He's the

01:05:11.908 --> 01:05:13.951
Second son of Lee Hak-seung,
the Chairman of Ewoo Shipping.

01:05:14.035 --> 01:05:14.952
What?

01:05:16.037 --> 01:05:16.996
Brian.

01:05:17.079 --> 01:05:18.372
Born Lee In-mu.

01:05:18.456 --> 01:05:19.415
Uh…

01:05:19.498 --> 01:05:20.374
He studied at a seminary in Canada.

01:05:21.876 --> 01:05:22.752
Five years ago,

01:05:22.835 --> 01:05:25.588
He was kicked out for passing
out cocaine to the churchgoers.

01:05:27.298 --> 01:05:28.215
At Ewoo Shipping,

01:05:28.299 --> 01:05:30.176
He didn't get much recognition
while his brother got promoted.

01:05:30.259 --> 01:05:31.177
He just got passed over.

01:05:31.761 --> 01:05:33.346
Create a new file about Ewoo Shipping.

01:05:33.429 --> 01:05:34.597
Hold on. There's more here.

01:05:34.680 --> 01:05:35.806
This guy was charged

01:05:35.890 --> 01:05:37.183
For manslaughter, it says.

01:05:37.266 --> 01:05:38.643
Six people died the night in question.

01:05:39.393 --> 01:05:41.354
- Heart attacks.
- Wait.

01:05:41.437 --> 01:05:42.355
Lee Hak-seung died the exact same way.

01:05:45.191 --> 01:05:47.318
Brian's defense was like the
Avengers, total dream team.

01:05:47.401 --> 01:05:48.444
They got him acquitted.

01:05:48.527 --> 01:05:49.904
The press must've been silenced.

01:05:49.987 --> 01:05:50.905
Not much was written.

01:05:52.573 --> 01:05:53.491
Let me see.

01:06:04.877 --> 01:06:08.047
DIR. LEE AND MANAGING SUCCESS
"MY BUSINESS PHILOSOPHY BASED ON FAITH"

01:06:55.177 --> 01:06:56.846
DIRECTOR

01:07:02.768 --> 01:07:03.686
Yes, director.

01:07:03.769 --> 01:07:04.687
Um, uh…

01:07:05.354 --> 01:07:06.480
Uh, sir…

