You claim you're him. But
I'm just not convinced.

01:32:32.296 --> 01:32:33.464
Oh, damn it all.

01:32:35.466 --> 01:32:36.509
Well, I realize now…

01:32:38.970 --> 01:32:40.263
These are paranoid ramblings.

01:32:42.056 --> 01:32:43.307
There's no rational.

01:33:00.866 --> 01:33:02.743
My god says total salvation…

01:33:03.536 --> 01:33:05.913
Is earned by more than faith
or simple conviction alone.

01:33:05.997 --> 01:33:07.123
You need more than these things.

01:33:07.999 --> 01:33:09.500
Lee-Hak-seung, however,

01:33:09.584 --> 01:33:11.252
Always insisted that we could be saved

01:33:11.335 --> 01:33:12.420
By faith alone.

01:33:13.379 --> 01:33:16.132
When a man places his
faith in the wrong thing,

01:33:17.091 --> 01:33:20.052
He might as well have an
incurable disease eating at his soul.

01:33:20.136 --> 01:33:22.054
So, when you're dealing
with a man like that,

01:33:28.311 --> 01:33:30.563
Death is the only thing that can cure him.

01:33:31.355 --> 01:33:32.315
In any case,

01:33:33.816 --> 01:33:36.777
Well you're the one who
upended this deal of ours hm?

01:33:36.861 --> 01:33:37.862
So from now on,

01:33:39.405 --> 01:33:40.573
We're doing things my way.

01:33:41.365 --> 01:33:42.491
Huh?

01:33:42.575 --> 01:33:43.409
Oh, you're tricky.

01:33:44.201 --> 01:33:45.786
Playing the holier-than-thou bastard.

01:33:46.454 --> 01:33:48.748
You finally show me all your true colors,

01:33:48.831 --> 01:33:49.915
Huh?

01:33:49.999 --> 01:33:51.250
Why?

01:33:51.334 --> 01:33:53.085
Because you think you all scare me? Huh?

01:33:54.170 --> 01:33:55.046
We're not done…

01:33:55.129 --> 01:33:56.380
But I need to check on something.

01:33:57.465 --> 01:33:58.299
So, you guys should all take a seat.

01:33:59.550 --> 01:34:00.635
It's rude to be standing

01:34:00.718 --> 01:34:01.844
If you've got a guest over.

01:34:02.928 --> 01:34:03.888
I said sit down.

01:34:03.971 --> 01:34:05.014
I mean it!

01:34:05.097 --> 01:34:06.015
You assholes!

01:34:06.974 --> 01:34:07.892
Shit.

01:34:18.861 --> 01:34:19.779
What is that?

01:34:22.031 --> 01:34:22.948
Huh?

01:34:24.617 --> 01:34:25.826
Come one, what is it?

01:34:28.454 --> 01:34:29.372
It's something I was supposed

01:34:29.455 --> 01:34:30.373
To bring from Mr. Lee.

01:34:36.504 --> 01:34:38.297
How come you said you
don't know what it is,

01:34:38.381 --> 01:34:39.298
If it's from you, huh?

01:34:51.102 --> 01:34:52.019
Okay, open it.

01:34:56.524 --> 01:34:57.441
Slowly.

01:35:01.654 --> 01:35:03.364
What is it? Ah, shit.

01:35:06.033 --> 01:35:07.034
Ah shit.

01:35:07.118 --> 01:35:08.035
Fuck me.

01:35:12.289 --> 01:35:14.041
MR. LEE

01:35:58.794 --> 01:35:59.712
Shit.

01:36:18.314 --> 01:36:19.231
Shit.

01:36:31.911 --> 01:36:33.704
Damn it, you fucking devil.

01:36:57.478 --> 01:36:58.395
Hold up.

01:37:15.162 --> 01:37:16.080
C'mere.

01:37:20.251 --> 01:37:22.086
You… Son of a bitch.

01:37:23.796 --> 01:37:24.839
Get up, you asshole.

01:37:24.922 --> 01:37:25.840
I'll show…

01:37:39.937 --> 01:37:40.813
- Stay still you asshole!
- On your knees.

01:37:40.896 --> 01:37:42.022
- Hands up!
- Get down!

01:37:42.106 --> 01:37:42.898
Stop!

01:37:42.982 --> 01:37:44.692
- Hands up! Hands up! I said get down!
- On your knees. Don't move.

01:37:44.775 --> 01:37:45.401
- Down!
- Now!

01:37:45.484 --> 01:37:46.151
Nobody move!

01:37:47.027 --> 01:37:47.945
Hurry, hurry.

01:37:48.946 --> 01:37:49.864
Masks off, all of you.

01:37:50.406 --> 01:37:51.323
Hurry up, assholes!

01:37:58.205 --> 01:37:59.123
You're kidding me, kids?

01:38:36.911 --> 01:38:37.953
Oh, shit.

01:38:45.002 --> 01:38:45.920
Hey!

01:38:48.172 --> 01:38:49.089
Are you okay?

01:38:51.717 --> 01:38:53.552
Someone came and took
Brian, I don't know where to.

01:38:54.219 --> 01:38:55.137
So-yeon.

01:38:55.220 --> 01:38:56.889
Yes! I'm alright, sir.

01:38:56.972 --> 01:38:57.848
You take the emergency staircase.

01:38:57.932 --> 01:38:59.224
- Yes, sir.
- You, come with me.

01:38:59.308 --> 01:39:00.059
- Yes, sir.
- Go.

01:39:14.198 --> 01:39:15.115
Listen here.

01:39:15.866 --> 01:39:16.784
Director.

01:39:21.789 --> 01:39:22.706
You…

01:39:24.208 --> 01:39:25.084
So you really thought

01:39:26.293 --> 01:39:28.128
You could just take over the
mantle of Mr. Lee like that?

01:39:31.507 --> 01:39:32.424
Seo Young-rak, sir…

01:39:45.229 --> 01:39:46.146
You know…

01:39:47.106 --> 01:39:49.024
You did almost kill me
in the factory fire.

01:39:50.776 --> 01:39:52.152
You actually could've become Mr. Lee.

01:39:54.989 --> 01:39:55.990
How that must hurt.

01:40:12.256 --> 01:40:13.173
Hey.

01:40:14.341 --> 01:40:15.718
This doesn't make any sense.

01:40:21.056 --> 01:40:21.974
What?

01:40:28.230 --> 01:40:29.148
Nine, right?

01:40:31.734 --> 01:40:33.694
I remember hearing about nine total,

01:40:33.777 --> 01:40:34.820
So there were at least that many

01:40:36.947 --> 01:40:38.699
All insisting that they were Mr. Lee.

01:40:42.703 --> 01:40:44.747
Even if hundreds made the
claim, I wouldn't have really cared.

01:40:46.915 --> 01:40:49.168
They say Korean people
inherit a paternal liar gene.

01:40:51.003 --> 01:40:52.671
Since our lives can be so difficult,

01:40:53.714 --> 01:40:55.758
We want to feel
compensated in some small way.

01:40:58.802 --> 01:41:00.304
Oh depressing, isn't it?

01:41:01.430 --> 01:41:02.347
Hmm?

01:41:05.601 --> 01:41:07.102
The other imposters were
all just talk, though.

01:41:09.730 --> 01:41:11.774
No, none of the others
were ever as brazen as you.

01:41:13.067 --> 01:41:14.068
I was surprised, I gotta say.

01:41:21.033 --> 01:41:22.367
And I was pretty curious.

01:41:27.748 --> 01:41:29.541
Who might this crazy asshole be

01:41:35.714 --> 01:41:36.632
That way.

01:41:45.015 --> 01:41:46.683
Lee Hak-seung and Chairwoman Oh…

01:41:48.143 --> 01:41:50.062
At the end of the day, I
can live without those two.

01:41:51.855 --> 01:41:52.773
It is what it is.

01:41:53.774 --> 01:41:54.900
But the Incheon fire?

01:41:56.652 --> 01:41:58.862
You must've taken
inspiration from my previous work.

01:42:00.739 --> 01:42:02.282
You had the wrong mindset, though.

01:42:04.159 --> 01:42:05.285
You only thought about winning.

01:42:05.911 --> 01:42:07.204
Right?

01:42:07.287 --> 01:42:08.330
Without caring

01:42:08.413 --> 01:42:09.331
About the cash.

01:42:20.259 --> 01:42:22.094
I mean, if you're
gonna do it, do it right.

01:42:23.303 --> 01:42:25.848
I worked so hard to build my
reputation. You never worked for anything.

01:42:26.390 --> 01:42:28.642
No common sense or business sensibility.

01:42:30.477 --> 01:42:32.104
That's why your father never appreciated
you and why he always treated you like the

01:42:32.187 --> 01:42:33.856
idiot you are.

01:42:38.443 --> 01:42:39.820
Sir, wait… Please.

01:42:39.903 --> 01:42:40.529
Spare me.

01:42:42.322 --> 01:42:43.240
How about we…

01:42:45.450 --> 01:42:46.368
We could talk to God?

01:42:47.536 --> 01:42:48.453
Huh?

01:42:49.037 --> 01:42:49.955
Let me pray for you.

01:42:50.873 --> 01:42:51.790
No, thank you.

01:43:04.136 --> 01:43:05.846
I know you're a smart man, Director.

01:43:08.307 --> 01:43:10.225
But you made three serious mistakes.

01:43:12.227 --> 01:43:13.979
You murdered Yook Pil-soon,
who spent her whole life…

01:43:14.771 --> 01:43:15.772
Working like a dog.

01:43:19.359 --> 01:43:21.445
But she died with her hair
burnt to her scalp cause of you.

01:43:25.741 --> 01:43:27.201
Do you know what I thought when I saw her?

01:43:30.621 --> 01:43:32.122
"I hope it got her quickly.

01:43:35.584 --> 01:43:37.294
I hope she burned before she knew it,

01:43:37.377 --> 01:43:38.754
Burned too fast to feel it."

01:43:44.051 --> 01:43:45.177
As for my dog, though,

01:43:45.260 --> 01:43:46.803
He couldn't even die.

01:43:47.846 --> 01:43:49.348
His back is all burned up.

01:43:51.433 --> 01:43:53.769
Everything melted, from his
intestines down to his anus.

01:43:56.730 --> 01:43:57.648
He survived

01:43:58.357 --> 01:43:59.441
And made it through the agony.

01:44:05.906 --> 01:44:07.074
Where you went wrong though…

01:44:09.493 --> 01:44:10.410
Well…

01:44:11.912 --> 01:44:13.580
Was thinking you could replace me.

01:44:16.250 --> 01:44:18.085
The sheer bravado of saying you were Lee…

01:44:19.378 --> 01:44:20.295
To me too.

01:44:28.512 --> 01:44:29.429
You scared?

01:44:36.561 --> 01:44:37.479
Does it hurt?

01:44:40.732 --> 01:44:43.110
Motherfucker, you scared now?

01:45:01.211 --> 01:45:02.754
MR. LEE

01:45:02.838 --> 01:45:03.755
Shit.

01:45:07.467 --> 01:45:08.385
I told you,

01:45:09.219 --> 01:45:10.137
I believed in you.

01:45:10.929 --> 01:45:11.888
You got him in the end.

01:45:14.516 --> 01:45:15.434
You little shit.

01:45:16.768 --> 01:45:17.728
Mr. Lee

01:45:17.811 --> 01:45:18.812
Will see you on the first floor.

01:45:20.564 --> 01:45:21.481
Shit.

01:45:26.486 --> 01:45:29.781
The train to Yeosu Expo Station
departs at three twenty-five p.m.

01:45:29.865 --> 01:45:33.118
The next train on the Gyeongin line
departs at three thirty-five p.m.

01:45:33.201 --> 01:45:36.204
The next train on the
Gyeongui Line departs at three…

01:45:39.624 --> 01:45:41.293
- Whoa, look out!
- Dear God!

01:45:41.376 --> 01:45:42.294
Damn!

01:45:42.377 --> 01:45:43.295
Help!

01:45:45.922 --> 01:45:46.965
Hey!

01:45:47.049 --> 01:45:47.966
Move, move!

01:46:09.196 --> 01:46:10.113
Laika.

01:46:13.075 --> 01:46:13.992
Ambulance!

01:46:21.875 --> 01:46:22.709
What's the dog's name?

01:46:24.419 --> 01:46:25.337
Jindo Dog.

01:46:26.254 --> 01:46:27.339
He's no Jindo.

01:46:31.802 --> 01:46:33.011
What's he named Jindo for?

01:46:33.845 --> 01:46:34.679
He's not a Jindo dog.

01:46:40.394 --> 01:46:41.436
I just like Jindos dogs.

01:47:10.799 --> 01:47:11.716
Jindo Dog.

01:47:12.509 --> 01:47:13.427
Hey!

01:47:14.511 --> 01:47:15.470
Jindo Dog.

01:47:15.554 --> 01:47:16.471
Hey.

01:47:24.146 --> 01:47:25.063
Laika.

01:47:38.702 --> 01:47:39.619
Hmm.

01:48:01.141 --> 01:48:02.184
The man

01:48:02.267 --> 01:48:03.435
Who calls himself Mr. Lee, and his gang,

01:48:03.518 --> 01:48:04.352
Have been arrested.

01:48:05.145 --> 01:48:07.397
We've seized twenty
kilograms of a new drug called Laika

01:48:07.481 --> 01:48:08.857
And batches of other drugs worth

01:48:08.940 --> 01:48:09.858
Thirty billion won

01:48:09.941 --> 01:48:10.817
In the market.

01:48:10.901 --> 01:48:11.902
This man

01:48:11.985 --> 01:48:13.487
Who called himself Mr. Lee

01:48:13.570 --> 01:48:16.114
Is heir to a prominent
shipping conglomerate.

01:48:16.698 --> 01:48:17.991
Lee and his gang

01:48:18.074 --> 01:48:19.493
Used a popular train station

01:48:19.576 --> 01:48:20.619
As a hub for

01:48:20.702 --> 01:48:21.703
Producing

01:48:21.786 --> 01:48:23.038
And distributing these drugs.

01:48:24.414 --> 01:48:26.500
LEE OF EWOO SHIPPING
DRUG LORD MR. LEE

01:48:27.334 --> 01:48:28.793
Front page of the finance papers.

01:48:29.628 --> 01:48:31.963
I already told you, he isn't Mr. Lee, sir.

01:48:32.047 --> 01:48:33.548
He confessed that he was.

01:48:34.591 --> 01:48:35.509
It's not a confession.

01:48:35.592 --> 01:48:37.177
That was just a bogus claim.

01:48:37.260 --> 01:48:38.094
Let's see here,

01:48:39.513 --> 01:48:41.139
How… long have you worked here?

01:48:42.098 --> 01:48:43.016
Thirteen years, I think?

01:48:44.559 --> 01:48:45.936
And you still haven't learned anything.

01:48:47.312 --> 01:48:48.396
Ouch…

01:48:48.480 --> 01:48:49.606
What? You said

01:48:49.689 --> 01:48:51.024
Lee's the dealer you
were running around with?

01:48:51.107 --> 01:48:52.484
You don't even know what his real name is.

01:48:53.652 --> 01:48:55.987
You said you don't even know
if he's Chinese or Japanese.

01:48:56.071 --> 01:48:57.197
Right?

01:48:57.280 --> 01:48:59.574
So, a Mr. Lee who says he's
"Mr. Lee" is making false claims.

01:48:59.658 --> 01:49:02.744
And the real "Mr. Lee" is the kid who was
on my narcotics team. But you don't know

01:49:02.827 --> 01:49:06.164
where he's from or what his name is, and
yet you still believe you'll catch him.

01:49:06.248 --> 01:49:07.457
Well?

01:49:07.541 --> 01:49:08.375
Does that about sum it up?

01:49:09.501 --> 01:49:11.920
What we owe the people is a
conclusion, not the full answer.

01:49:12.003 --> 01:49:12.879
Got it?

01:49:12.963 --> 01:49:14.422
Oh, I see what she meant now.

01:49:14.506 --> 01:49:15.757
What now?

01:49:15.840 --> 01:49:17.217
I'd wondered what she meant when she said,

01:49:19.386 --> 01:49:20.345
"The world is shit,

01:49:20.428 --> 01:49:21.513
That's what I do drugs for."

01:49:22.180 --> 01:49:23.431
What the hell are you saying…

01:49:24.975 --> 01:49:25.892
Huh?

01:49:27.185 --> 01:49:28.019
Hey punk, where're you going?

01:49:28.979 --> 01:49:29.980
To look for a dog.

01:49:38.113 --> 01:49:39.030
Captain Jo.

01:49:39.698 --> 01:49:41.449
We're reorganizing our evidence files.

01:49:42.909 --> 01:49:44.035
Let's start over together.

01:49:45.161 --> 01:49:46.413
The case is closed, you guys.

01:49:46.496 --> 01:49:47.414
It's all over.

01:49:48.832 --> 01:49:50.292
Go home, wash up,

01:49:50.375 --> 01:49:51.960
And try to get some real sleep.

01:49:55.088 --> 01:49:56.006
When you

01:49:57.007 --> 01:49:58.758
Chase something like
hell for years and years,

01:50:00.218 --> 01:50:02.262
You start to wonder what
it even is you're chasing

01:50:02.345 --> 01:50:04.097
And why you're chasing
it in the first place.

01:50:06.349 --> 01:50:07.267
At times like that,

01:50:08.310 --> 01:50:10.604
You gotta go home,
clean up and get into bed.

01:50:11.605 --> 01:50:12.522
So-

01:50:19.821 --> 01:50:20.739
I hope you all…

01:50:22.282 --> 01:50:24.284
Keep your hearts and never
become completely jaded.

01:50:30.498 --> 01:50:31.499
Thanks for all your hard work.

01:52:28.575 --> 01:52:29.743
Laika!

01:53:20.418 --> 01:53:21.920
You put a tracker on Laika?

01:53:23.505 --> 01:53:24.464
What were you thinking there?

01:53:27.050 --> 01:53:28.259
In case I couldn't find you otherwise.

01:53:32.931 --> 01:53:34.474
Don't you believe in yourself, Captain Jo?

01:53:39.562 --> 01:53:40.855
How'd you get all the way out here?

01:53:45.318 --> 01:53:46.236
Good question.

01:53:49.823 --> 01:53:51.199
Look, you're a very good man.

01:53:56.120 --> 01:53:57.455
But Mr. Lee is dead now.

01:53:58.581 --> 01:53:59.791
Officially, yes, the case is.

01:54:01.042 --> 01:54:02.168
But aren't you still alive?

01:54:09.300 --> 01:54:10.218
Tell me.

01:54:13.263 --> 01:54:14.180
Who am I?

01:54:20.353 --> 01:54:21.563
I don't even know the answer.

01:54:27.193 --> 01:54:28.653
When I was in that shipping container…

01:54:30.738 --> 01:54:31.948
I was with my parents, at first.

01:54:36.536 --> 01:54:38.663
While we were being
smuggled, they overdosed and died.

01:54:40.874 --> 01:54:41.791
Both of them.

01:54:43.585 --> 01:54:44.502
In front of me.

01:54:55.722 --> 01:54:56.764
What will you do now, Jo?

01:55:09.694 --> 01:55:10.612
Want some coffee?

01:56:19.973 --> 01:56:21.933
You ever been happy in your life?

01:58:28.309 --> 01:58:35.108
IN LOVING MEMORY OF KIM JU-HYUK
